here for the  given array if we want to find maximum sum of the subarray our brute force approach would be 
for(int i=0;i<n;i++>){
        sum =0;
    for(int j=i;j<n;j++>){
       sum = sum+arr[i];
       max sum = Math.max(sum,maxsum);
    }
}
here in every iteration we calculate sum of every subarray and compare
time complexity woukld be o(nsquare)
hence we use kadanes algorithm to enhance and decrease the timecomplexity to o(n)
in this we keep track of the maximum sum so far and the current sum at each index if the current sum becomes negative we reset it to 0 and continue to the next index
let us see the code for kadanes algorithm
for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
    currentSum = currentSum + arr[i];
    if(currentSum > maxSum){
        maxSum = currentSum;
    }
    if(currentSum < 0){
        currentSum = 0;
    }
}
in this we should not intialize maxsum as 0 because if all the elements are negative then the maximum sum would be the maximum element in the array which is negative so we should initialize maxsum as Integer.MIN_VALUE
or we can initialize maxsum as arr[0] and currentSum as 0 